# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env` for local development, and set the same variables as Server
# Variables in the Vercel project settings. `.env` is git-ignored.
#
# Nothing here is required to build the site: without RESEND_API_KEY and
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL the build still succeeds and POST /api/contact returns a
# 503 that points visitors at the email address instead of pretending to send.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Analytics ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Plausible is cookie-free, so there is no consent banner. Leave this unset to
# ship with analytics completely disabled; set it to the domain you added in the
# Plausible dashboard to enable it. Visitors can still opt out on
# /cookie-preferences either way.
# PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=linklyllc.com

# --- Contact form (server-only) ------------------------------------------------
# https://resend.com/api-keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# The address Resend sends from. Must be on a domain you have verified in
# Resend (a `onboarding@resend.dev` address only works for your own account).
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=website@linklyllc.com

# Where inquiries are delivered. Defaults to site.email in src/config/site.ts.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=hello@linklyllc.com
